  description:
  - 'An increase in metabolism has evolved the local species of hares to become hyperactive.
    Common observed behaviors include mass production of underground passage ways
    and an insatiable appetite, as well as increased fecundancy. '
  - It is estimated that the local hare population will double every 2 years, classifying
    this species as invasive.
  leftText: 
  rightText: An increase in metabolism has evolved the local species of hares to
    become hyperactive. Common observed behaviors include mass production of underground
    passage ways and an insatiable appetite, as well as increased fecundancy. It
    is estimated that the local hare population will double every 2 years, classifying
    this species as invasive.
